🎯 WHAT AM I BUILDING?

A responsive e-commerce website where users can browse, search, filter, sort, view product details, add products to a cart, change quantities, checkout, and receive an order confirmation.

🧱 HTML — STRUCTURE

HTML = structure/skeleton of the website.

Used for:

Navigation
Headings/text
Images
Buttons
Product cards
Search/filter controls
Cart
Checkout form

Say: “I used HTML to create the structure and content of my website.”

🎨 CSS — DESIGN

CSS = how the website looks.

Used for:

Colors
Fonts
Spacing
Layout
Buttons
Product cards
Hover effects
Forms
Responsive design

Responsive = website adapts to desktop, tablet and mobile.
Uses media queries.

Say: “I used CSS for the visual design and responsive layout.”

⚙️ JAVASCRIPT — FUNCTIONALITY

JavaScript = makes the website interactive.

Used for:

Search
Filtering
Sorting
Fetching products
Product details
Cart
Quantities
Totals
Form validation
Updating the page

Say: “I used JavaScript to add functionality and user interaction.”

🌐 API

API = allows my website to communicate with another service and retrieve data.

My website → API → product data → JavaScript → webpage.

🧪 DUMMYJSON

DummyJSON = the external API providing my product data.

Instead of creating a backend/database myself, I retrieve products from DummyJSON. The project specifically requires using the API instead of hardcoding all products.

Say: “I used the DummyJSON API to retrieve product data and dynamically display it on my website.”

📡 fetch()

Fetch = request/get data from the API.

⏳ async/await

Allows JavaScript to wait for the API response.

🚨 try/catch

Handles errors if something goes wrong with the API request.

⏳ LOADING STATE

Shows “Loading products…” while waiting for the API.

🔎 filter()

Keeps only items that match a condition.

Used for:

Search
Category filtering
↕️ sort()

Arranges items.

Used for:

Price low → high
Price high → low
Name A → Z
Name Z → A
🔍 find()

Finds one specific item.

Used to find a product by its ID.

🔄 map()

Transforms each item into something else.

Can be used to create product-card HTML.

🔁 forEach()

Does something for every item.

➕ reduce()

Combines many values into one result.

Used to calculate the cart total.

🌳 DOM

DOM = JavaScript's way of interacting with the HTML.

Important methods:

querySelector()
querySelectorAll()
getElementById()
textContent
innerHTML
classList
🖱️ EVENTS

Events = things the user does.

click → buttons
input → search
change → dropdowns
submit → checkout form
📦 ARRAY

Stores multiple things.

products = [product1, product2, product3]

🧍 OBJECT

Describes one thing.

product = { id, title, price }

🧠 VARIABLE

A named container that stores information.

🔀 CONDITION

Allows JavaScript to make decisions.

if (...) { ... }

🧩 FUNCTION

A reusable set of instructions.

🏹 ARROW FUNCTION

A shorter/modern way to write a function.

💾 LOCALSTORAGE

Browser storage used to remember the cart.

Add product → save cart → refresh → cart remains.

setItem() → save
getItem() → retrieve
removeItem() → delete
📋 JSON

Used when storing/transferring data.

JSON.stringify() → convert data for storage
JSON.parse() → convert it back
🛒 CART FLOW

Add to Cart → cart array → localStorage → cart counter → quantity changes → total → checkout → validation → confirmation → clear cart.